LOCAL PATCH (2026-10-09, KaChat-Desktop Build 134)
  kaspa/kaspa.js and cipher/cipher.js: __wbg_newnoargs answers "return this" with a function that
  returns globalThis instead of `new Function(...)`. The page's CSP (tools/security-headers.mjs)
  has no 'unsafe-eval', and js-sys / workflow-rs build exactly that string to reach the global
  object; the SDK's websocket reconnect timer threw "EvalError ... 'unsafe-eval' is not an allowed
  source of script" after a failed node connection. Any other string still goes to Function and is
  refused by the CSP. The .wasm binaries are unchanged; the .js checksums in SHA256SUMS were
  updated for this patch (bash tools/check-wasm.sh --update).

LOCAL PATCH (2026-10-13, KaChat-Desktop Build 145)
  The same __wbg_newnoargs in kaspa/kaspa.js and cipher/cipher.js also answers workflow-core's
  promise-with-resolvers helper ("let resolve, reject; const p = new Promise(...); p.resolve =
  resolve; p.reject = reject; return p;", compared with whitespace collapsed) with a plain function
  instead of `new Function(...)`: a timer callback built it and threw the same CSP EvalError. Both
  .wasm binaries hold exactly that snippet and "return this"; nothing else reaches Function. The
  .wasm binaries are unchanged; the .js checksums were updated (bash tools/check-wasm.sh --update).

LOCAL PATCH (2026-10-13, KaChat-Desktop Build 148)
  kaspa/kaspa.js only: __wbg_newnoargs also answers workflow-core's requestAnimationFrame fallback
  ("if (!this.requestAnimationFrame){ ... setImmediate ... setTimeout(callback, 0) }", whitespace
  collapsed) without eval. It was the third and last JS snippet kaspa_bg.wasm passes to Function
